        "original_id": "5f681713-8bcf-5568-a27c-f003e8661c6f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ann Wilson\n- Organizations: Hit Parader\n- Products: \"Daze Gone By\", \"The Wild Bunch\"\n- Groups: Antix, Slayer, Lizzy Borden, Megadeth, Anthrax, Raven, Grim Reaper\n- Topics: heavy metal vocalist rankings\n\nFacts:\n- Hit Parader was an American music magazine that operated from 1942 to 2008.\n- In 1984, Antix's song \"Daze Gone By\" appeared on Hit Parader's compilation album \"The Wild Bunch.\"\n- \"The Wild Bunch\" also included bands such as Slayer, Lizzy Borden, Megadeth, Anthrax, Raven, and Grim Reaper.\n- In 2006, Hit Parader listed Ann Wilson as one of the \"Top Heavy Metal Vocalists of All Time.\"",
